To create an HbbTV website that streams an M3U8 file, you can use HTML5 and the [HLS.js](https://github.com/video-dev/hls.js) library. This approach ensures compatibility with HbbTV devices that may not support native HLS playback. Below is a complete example of how to implement this:

---

### ✅ **HbbTV M3U8 Streaming Website**

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>HbbTV HLS Stream</title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
</head>
<body>
    <!-- Video element to display the stream -->
    <video id="video" controls autoplay></video>

    <!-- Include HLS.js library from a CDN -->
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/hls.js@latest"></script>
    <script>
        // Get the video element
        const video = document.getElementById('video');

        // Check if HLS.js is supported
        if (Hls.isSupported()) {
            const hls = new Hls();
            hls.loadSource('stream.m3u8'); // Replace with your M3U8 URL
            hls.attachMedia(video);
            hls.on(Hls.Events.MANIFEST_PARSED, function () {
                video.play().catch(error => {
                    console.error("Playback failed:", error);
                });
            });
        } 
        // Fallback for browsers with native HLS support
        else if (video.canPlayType('application/x-mpegURL') || 
                 video.canPlayType('application/vnd.apple.mpegurl')) {
            video.src = 'stream.m3u8'; // Replace with your M3U8 URL
            video.addEventListener('loadedmetadata', () => {
                video.play().catch(error => {
                    console.error("Playback failed:", error);
                });
            });
        } else {
            console.warn("HLS playback not supported in this browser.");
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

### 📌 **Key Notes**

1. **M3U8 URL**:  
   Replace `'stream.m3u8'` with the actual URL of your HLS stream. Ensure the URL is accessible (e.g., via HTTPS) and properly configured with CORS headers if needed.

2. **HTTPS Requirement**:  
   HbbTV devices often require secure connections. Serve your HTML and M3U8 files over HTTPS.

3. **CORS Headers**:  
   If the M3U8 file is hosted on a different domain, ensure the server includes these headers:
   ```http
   Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
   Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, OPTIONS
   Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Origin, Content-Type, Accept
   ```

4. **HbbTV Compatibility**:  
   HbbTV devices may use older browsers. Test your implementation on a supported device or emulator to ensure compatibility.

5. **Fallback Handling**:  
   The script checks for native HLS support (e.g., Safari) and falls back to HLS.js if needed. This ensures broader compatibility.

---

